# Parameters applied ONLY in SITL (scripts/sim.sh), never on hardware.
# Each one relaxes a safety check that exists for a real vehicle but has no
# meaning in an unattended simulation.

# Data-link-loss failsafe off: SITL runs without a ground station, and with
# NAV_DLL_ACT > 0 PX4 refuses to arm ("Preflight Fail: No connection to the GCS").
# On hardware keep this enabled and fly with a GCS link.
NAV_DLL_ACT 0

# Magnetometer: PX4's own simulator (sensor_mag_sim: WMM field at the
# ground-truth position, rotated by the ground-truth attitude) instead of
# Gazebo Harmonic's, which is not usable in tilted flight; see
# firmware/px4_patches/0002-* and quad-autonomy-sim's phase 2 write-up.
SENS_EN_MAGSIM 1

# Magnetic declination [deg] for flights without GPS (EKF2 cannot look it up).
# Must equal the WMM value sensor_mag_sim uses at the world origin; measured
# against ground truth in quad-autonomy-sim's phase 2. On hardware: the
# site's declination (or let EKF2 derive it from GPS).
EKF2_MAG_DECL 3.54
# Declination source. In PX4 v1.17 EKF2 only uses EKF2_MAG_DECL when bit 1
# (SAVE_GEO_DECL) is set (mag_control.cpp, getMagDeclination); with 0 it uses a
# declination of 0 regardless of EKF2_MAG_DECL. 2 = use EKF2_MAG_DECL.
EKF2_DECL_TYPE 2

# The simulated magnetometer has no hard-iron offset, but PX4 saves the mag
# biases EKF2 "learns" into the calibration at every disarm (SENS_MAG_AUTOCAL).
# Fed bad data once, that made every later flight worse; keep SITL
# calibration at zero and fixed.
SENS_MAG_AUTOCAL 0
CAL_MAG0_XOFF 0.0
CAL_MAG0_YOFF 0.0
CAL_MAG0_ZOFF 0.0

# GPS delay compensation off: PX4's simulated GPS (sensor_gps_sim) stamps each
# fix with the true sample time and adds no latency, but EKF2 assumed the
# hardware default of 110 ms and so ran ~0.1 s AHEAD of ground truth (measured
# against both Gazebo's and PX4's ground truth in quad-autonomy-sim: ~0.15 m at 1.5 m/s,
# drawn into the map as displaced surfaces). PX4's own SIH airframes set 0 for
# the same reason. On hardware keep the receiver's real latency (default 110).
EKF2_GPS_DELAY 0

# uXRCE-DDS timestamp synchronisation off. With it on, the client converts
# PX4 time to the agent's wall clock. In SITL PX4 time follows the simulation
# clock, so whenever Gazebo runs below real time the converted stamps stretch
# and are corrected in steps. Measured with two agents and the device camera
# (RTF ~0.85), per agent per flight: 8,139 IMU samples, none missing, but
# stamped across 131 s for a 98 s flight, with 169-185 apparent gaps and 7-8
# jumps over 100 ms. The ESKF bridged each "gap" and re-anchored on each jump,
# and in the worst runs drifted by a metre. Off: 0 gaps, 0 steps, and every
# PX4 stamp is raw PX4 time = simulation time, the same clock as /clock.
# Messages sent to PX4 are unaffected (they use timestamp 0: stamp on arrival).
# On hardware keep it on: there PX4 and the companion both run in real time.
UXRCE_DDS_SYNCT 0
